 8 (MIT)
DESCRIPTION:An academic-year fellowship at MIT for journalists covering sci
 ence\, health\, technology or the environment\, with seminars\, MIT and Ha
 rvard courses and a self-directed study project. ELIGIBILITY: full-time st
 aff or freelance journalists with at least 3 consecutive years of science\
 , health\, technology or environment coverage\; international applicants w
 elcome.\n\nOrganisation: Knight Science Journalism Program at MIT\nLocatio
 n: Cambridge\, Massachusetts\, USA (in residence for the academic year). I
 nternational applicants welcome\; MIT sponsors a J-1 visa.\nAward: USD 87\
 ,500 stipend over 9.5 months\, plus USD 5\,000 for travel and housing\, he
 alth insurance and a childcare subsidy. No application fee.\nDuration: Aca
 demic year 2027-28\, about 9.5 months.\n\nMore: https://ksj.mit.edu/fellow
 ships/academic-year-fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
